        "original_id": "150c172b-3b33-5275-9c17-10629542479f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ronnie Radke, Dave Brockie, Lloyd Kaufman, Debbie Rochon\n- Bands: Gwar, Death Piggy, X-Cops, Dave Brockie Experience, Falling in Reverse, Escape the Fate\n- Tours: Bury the Hatchet Tour\n- TV and Films: Holliston, Hack Job\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, entertainer, record producer, lead vocalist, bassist\n\nFacts:\n- Ronald Joseph Radke was born on December 15, 1983, in Las Vegas, Nevada.\n- Ronnie Radke is an American singer, songwriter, entertainer, and record producer.\n- David Murray Brockie was born on August 30, 1963, and died on March 23, 2014.\n- Dave Brockie was a Canadian musician best known as the lead vocalist of Gwar, where he performed as Oderus Urungus.\n- Dave Brockie performed as a bassist and lead singer in Death Piggy, X-Cops, and the Dave Brockie Experience.\n- Dave Brockie starred in the comedy-horror TV sitcom \"Holliston\" as Oderus Urungus.\n- The Bury the Hatchet Tour was the first time Falling in Reverse and Escape the Fate joined forces after Ronnie Radke was kicked from Escape the Fate.\n- Hack Job stars Dave Brockie, Lloyd Kaufman, and Debbie Rochon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
